Better:

@Entity tells Hibernate that this Java class participates in ORM and should be managed/mapped as an entity.


pom.xml

Your version:

This tells the ORM about dependencies.

Better:

pom.xml tells Maven which libraries my Java project needs, such as Hibernate and the PostgreSQL JDBC driver. Maven makes those libraries available to the application.



hibernate.cfg.xml

Your version:

This contains credentials required to connect Java to the database.

Better:

hibernate.cfg.xml provides Hibernate with configuration information, including database URL, username, password, JDBC driver, and other Hibernate settings.

